{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Blessed be the fruit of your body.</b> Here in the blessings He placed the blessing of the body before the blessing of food, for afterward He says, ברוך טנאך (your basket). But in the curses He placed טנאך first and afterward פרי בטנך, to teach you that He punishes a person first in his property, and if he repents, well and good; and if not, He punishes him in his body. And so they said in the Midrash: the Merciful One does not exact retribution from persons first."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:32.223175111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}